## 4. Deprecation & Versioning Policy (`CT8`)

- **One-Version Rule within a major prefix (`/api/v1/...`)**: Do not proliferate `/api/v1.1`, `/api/v2`, `/api/v3` for routine feature work. Evolve `/api/v1` additively using Expand-and-Contract.
- **Major version bump (`/api/v2/...`)**: Reserved strictly for structural domain rewrites approved via `D-NN` where Expand-and-Contract on `/api/v1` is impossible.
- **Deprecation headers & metadata**: Deprecated endpoints must set `deprecated=True` in the OpenAPI/schema declaration and emit RFC 8594 `Deprecation: true` and `Sunset: <HTTP-date>` headers with a `Link: <successor-url>; rel="successor-version"` header.

See [`references/01-conventions-schemas-and-idempotency.md`]({{ref_01}}) for DTO and pagination rules, and [`references/03-snapshot-handshake-and-review.md`]({{ref_03}}) for snapshot diffing and review severity gates.
